Student: write a function that slice an image into four from the center in flutter,  dart language

Tutor: In Flutter, you can create a function that slices an image into four parts from the center using the `Positioned` widget to position each of the four parts. These parts can be created using `Image` widget along with `ClipRect` to clip each part. Here's an example:

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() {
  runApp(MyApp());
}

class MyApp extends StatelessWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return MaterialApp(
      home: Scaffold(
        appBar: AppBar(
          title: Text("Slice Image Example"),
        ),
        body: Center(
          child: Container(
            width: 200,
            height: 200,
            child: Stack(
              children: _sliceImage("image_asset_name")),
          ),
        ),
      ),
    );
  }

  List<Widget> _sliceImage(String imageUrl) {
    return [
      // Top-left part
      Positioned(
        top: 0,
        left: 0,
        child: ClipRect(
          child: Align(
            alignment: Alignment.topLeft,
            widthFactor: 0.5,
            heightFactor: 0.5,
            child: Image.asset(imageUrl),
          ),
        ),
      ),
      // Top-right part
      Positioned(
        top: 0,
        right: 0,
        child: ClipRect(
          child: Align(
            alignment: Alignment.topRight,
            widthFactor: 0.5,
            heightFactor: 0.5,
            child: Image.asset(imageUrl),
          ),
        ),
      ),
      // Bottom-left part
      Positioned(
        left: 0,
        bottom: 0,
        child: ClipRect(
          child: Align(
            alignment: Alignment.bottomLeft,
            widthFactor: 0.5,
            heightFactor: 0.5,
            child: Image.asset(imageUrl),
          ),
        ),
      ),
      /// Bottom-right part
      Positioned(
        right: 0,
        bottom: 0,
        child: ClipRect(
          child: Align(
            alignment: Alignment.bottomRight,
            widthFactor: 0.5,
            heightFactor: 0.5,
            child: Image.asset(imageUrl),
          ),
        ),
      ),
    ];
  }
}
```

Replace the `image_asset_name` with your actual image asset name. This function will return a list of four Positioned Widgets (Top-left part, Top-right part, Bottom-left part, Bottom-right part) which can be used as children of a Stack widget to position them.

